  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      "Greek has been written with its own alphabet for almost three thousand years. The word *alphabet* itself comes from its first two letters, *άλφα* and *βήτα*, and both the Latin and the Cyrillic alphabets grew out of it. You already know some letters from maths and science: π, Σ, Δ, Ω.",
      {
        "ul": [
          "There are 24 letters, and Greek is read almost exactly as it is written: once you know the letters and a few pairs, you can read any word aloud.",
          "Every letter has a capital and a small form, as in English: Α α, Μ μ, Τ τ.",
          "Sigma has two small forms: σ at the start or in the middle of a word, ς at the end: *σαλάτα*, *τέλος*.",
          "Almost every word has an accent mark (΄) on the vowel you stress: *σπίτι* is read *spí-ti*. Say that syllable a little louder."
        ]
      },
      "In this lesson you learn the four vowels and seven consonants that look like letters you already know. With them you can read your first words.",
      {
        "h": "The vowels"
      },
      "Greek vowels are short and clear, as in Italian or Spanish. Tap each letter to see how it sounds and a word that has it.",
      {
        "letters": [
          {
            "letter": "Α α",
            "latin": "a",
            "say": "like the a in father",
            "word": "μαμά",
            "word_latin": "mamá",
            "meaning": "mum"
          },
          {
            "letter": "Ε ε",
            "latin": "e",
            "say": "like the e in bed",
            "word": "μέλι",
            "word_latin": "méli",
            "meaning": "honey"
          },
          {
            "letter": "Ι ι",
            "latin": "i",
            "say": "like the ee in see, but short",
            "word": "σπίτι",
            "word_latin": "spíti",
            "meaning": "house"
          },
          {
            "letter": "Ο ο",
            "latin": "o",
            "say": "like the o in for, but short",
            "word": "κιλό",
            "word_latin": "kiló",
            "meaning": "kilo"
          }
        ],
        "lang": "el"
      },
      {
        "h": "Letters you already know"
